This is not nearly as bad as it may seem.

Prayer won't help you yet.

The fastest way out of a pit is to move diagonally until you're free,
but you don't want to take any chances with a q adjacent.

The /slow monster would be very nice, but you are stuck and it's not in
line of fire yet.

You _can_ engrave Elbereth while in a pit.

I would "E-Elbereth" this turn, and check it with :
If it worked, and the q was in line of fire, I'd zap him with /slow
monster.
If the first E failed, I'd try E again.
If my HP got low enough, I'd pray if possible.
As soon as he's turned to flee, is slow, and there are 2 squares
between us, I'd try climbing out of the pit.  Until then, I'd add 1
more finger-Elbereth each turn.



